IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sop-payments`

-- Building and Construction Industry Security of Payment Act 2004, ss 4, 8, 9, 10(2)(b), 11(1), 12, 13(3)(a), 15, 17(6), 18, 22, 24(3), 25, 26, 27, 36 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_building-and-construction-industry-security-of-payment-act-2004.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Day numbers are counts on the Act's calendar of days (s 2: public holidays excluded). Month numbers are one running scale.
-- The prescribed review amount (s 18(1)) and judgment-debt rate (s 8(5)(b)) are not in the deposit; 10000 and 5.33 are
-- placeholders chosen for the cases, not the prescribed figures.

§ `s 4`

#ASSERT `the contract is treated as made in writing` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the contract is treated as made in writing` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `the Act applies to the contract` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to the contract` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to the contract` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Act applies to the contract` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE

